## Dependencies

The MIT license above covers tonearm's own code. It does not cover the
following, which are used as-is and keep their own licenses:

### Vendored: roonapi 0.1.6

`scripts/vendor/roonapi/` is a vendored, unmodified copy of `roonapi` 0.1.6
from https://github.com/pavoni/pyroon, licensed **Apache License 2.0**. Its
own license text is retained in place at `scripts/vendor/roonapi/LICENSE` and
must not be altered. See `scripts/vendor/README.md` for why it is vendored
rather than installed as a system package, and how to refresh it.

### Runtime system dependencies

tonearm's daemon (`tonearmd`) requires two Python packages be present on the
system interpreter, installed separately (see `README.md`):

- `python-dbus-next` (MPRIS/D-Bus integration)
- `python-websocket-client` (the Roon MOO protocol transport, also a
  dependency of the vendored `roonapi`)

Neither is bundled with this repository; both are ordinary Arch/Omarchy
packages installed via `omarchy pkg add`.
